# The deconflate state files are append-only sets of (QID, viaf_dep) lines, read
# back into a deduping dict (order- and duplicate-independent). Merge them as a
# UNION so two machines (Toolforge + local) that each append their own runs never
# conflict -- git keeps both sides' lines; the reader dedupes. eol=lf keeps the
# committed content LF even when appended on Windows (Python text mode writes
# CRLF there), so cross-platform merges stay clean.
done.txt    merge=union eol=lf
review.txt  merge=union eol=lf
checked.txt merge=union eol=lf
error.txt   merge=union eol=lf
